@startuml error-model
set separator none
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam nodesep 20
skinparam ranksep 110
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor White
  BorderColor #555555
}
hide empty members
hide circle
hide stereotype

title transcript-mcp — Error Model: Where Errors Start → What Callers Receive
caption Library errors are translated by YtTranscriptApiBasedProvider. Each arrow shows the error a caller receives.

package "Library errors (youtube_transcript_api)" <<Folder>> #F5F5F5 {
  class YouTubeRequestFailed
  class VideoUnavailable
  class InvalidVideoId
  class AgeRestricted
  class NoTranscriptFound
  class TranscriptsDisabled
  class "any other exception" as AnyOther
}

package "Raised inside transcript" <<Folder>> #FFF6E0 {
  class TranscriptProviderManager
  class YtURLAttributeExtractorCoordinator
  class "mappers" as Mappers
}

package "transcript errors (exposed to callers)" <<Folder>> #EAF2FF {
  package "RetriableError (is_retriable = True)" <<Rectangle>> {
    class ServiceUnavailable
  }
  package "NonRetriableError (is_retriable = False)" <<Rectangle>> {
    class VideoNotFound
    class AuthRequired
    class TranscriptNotFound
    class UnknownException
    class NotSupportedError
    class InvalidLink
  }
  class DataError
}

package "Python built-in" <<Folder>> #F5F5F5 {
  class ValueError
}

note right of InvalidLink : defined, not raised

YouTubeRequestFailed --> ServiceUnavailable
VideoUnavailable --> VideoNotFound
InvalidVideoId --> VideoNotFound
AgeRestricted --> AuthRequired
NoTranscriptFound --> TranscriptNotFound
TranscriptsDisabled --> TranscriptNotFound
AnyOther --> UnknownException

TranscriptProviderManager --> NotSupportedError : no provider for URL
TranscriptProviderManager --> ValueError : empty URL
YtURLAttributeExtractorCoordinator --> ValueError : unrecognised URL
Mappers --> DataError : invalid upstream data
@enduml
